{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":673,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Neh.1","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Nehemiah","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Nehemiah 1","reference":"Nehemiah 1","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"Nehemiah is informed of the deplorable state of the Jews at Jerusalem, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"1-3.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"He fasts and prays, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"4-11","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"1.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":6,"text":"The words - Or rather, the acts, as the word often signifies.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":7,"text":"Chisleu - Which is the ninth month, containing part of November, and part of December.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":8,"text":"Year - Of Artaxerxes.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":9,"text":"Shushan - The royal city of Persia.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":10,"text":"3.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":11,"text":"The province - In Judea, now a province under the Persian monarchs.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":12,"text":"The wall, &c. - The walls and gates continue as Nebuchadnezzar left them; the Jews not being in a condition to rebuild them, nor having commission from the kings of Persia to do so.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":13,"text":"4.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":14,"text":"The God of heaven - Who seeth in secret; secret; having no opportunity of doing it openly.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":15,"text":"6.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":16,"text":"Which I pray, &c. - He refers to all the prayers, which he had for some time been putting up.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":17,"text":"11.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":18,"text":"To fear thy name - Those who truly desire to fear his name, shall be graciously accepted of God.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":19,"text":"This man - The king: who is but a man and therefore his heart is wholly at thy disposal. favour with men is then comfortable, when we see it springing from the mercy of God.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":20,"text":"Cup-bearer - Whereby I had opportunity to speak to him, and some favour with him.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Nehemiah","chapter":1}}